    {
      "id": "k_OKwdXEhFfHKQL9BL2hH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1763.0434342951967,
      "y": 21352.07090383637,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bOQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 149379755,
      "version": 1214,
      "versionNonce": 1712882537,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790692522346,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A lot of time what happened is, in case of designing a system, we try to over estimate the amount of\neffort that we might have to put in order to execute a task.\n\nNow a day, in lot of systems what we find is we have significant amount of machine capabilities \navailable, probably for our system we dont need to over designed anything that is technically not\neven required, just knowing the terms like sharding, partitioning, caching might not help alot\nin our interviews because we might throw these terms randomly here and there, eventually leading up\nto the fact that we might introduct things in the system which are probably not even required.\nthat what we are trying to get some lights on.\nand try to understand that what are the decent capabilities of the lot of machinaries available that\nwe can use, and we will talk about what kind of latency they actually provide in order to have a\ngood calculative call that we can take. in order to choose something over some other.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A lot of time what happened is, in case of designing a system, we try to over estimate the amount of\neffort that we might have to put in order to execute a task.\n\nNow a day, in lot of systems what we find is we have significant amount of machine capabilities \navailable, probably for our system we dont need to over designed anything that is technically not\neven required, just knowing the terms like sharding, partitioning, caching might not help alot\nin our interviews because we might throw these terms randomly here and there, eventually leading up\nto the fact that we might introduct things in the system which are probably not even required.\nthat what we are trying to get some lights on.\nand try to understand that what are the decent capabilities of the lot of machinaries available that\nwe can use, and we will talk about what kind of latency they actually provide in order to have a\ngood calculative call that we can take. in order to choose something over some other.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
